pendent: no fruiting bunches appear in render-0 or render-1. The date cluster (fn-111) is acknowledged as not landed."], "observations": ["render-0 and render-1 each show a single unbranched trunk with a rosette of pinnate fronds at the apex. There are no branches and no foliage on the trunk.", "The trunk is straight and vertical in render-0 and very slightly leaning in render-1. Its diameter is nearly constant, with a mild flare at the base in both seeds.", "The lowest fronds hang somewhat below the crown base in both seeds, but the droop is short and the crown overall reads as a ball rather than a fountain or shuttlecock.", "render-3 (P-BASE) is flagged visibility 'hidden' in the joint metadata. The visible pixels show a smooth trunk with about 5 sparse stubs and no ground contact region.", "Finish: the flat, clean shading is broadly at the level of the spruce anchor (anchor-0). The trunk surface has no texture detail. The anchor was used for finish quality only, not morphology.", "Foliage colour (deep green) is within the frond-colour-range variation seen in reference-0.", "The straight trunk is within the trunk-lean-and-curve variation (reference-1 and reference-2 are vertical). The owner requires straight or gently leaning.", "Epiphytes are absent from the render. This matches the owner's requirement, and epiphytes are classed as variation, not species character."], "findings": [{"observation": "Both seeds show a compact, dense crown of short fronds. It does not have the long, arching, recurving fronds of reference-0, and the lowest fronds droop only slightly.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size dials may still be too low, and rachis curvature may be too weak to produce the arching sweep."}, {"observation": "The leaflets are broad, soft and flat-lanceolate, not narrow, stiff and sharp-pointed. The frond margin does not look bristly or V-sectioned.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Leaflet width-to-length ratio and insertion angle variation may be off from palm values. Leaflets may also be drawn with a generic broadleaf blade shape."}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is smooth and untextured, with a few isolated small stubs. It has no spiral diamond lattice of leaf bases and no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The fn-110 trunk organs may be placed too sparsely and too small, so they do not tessellate into a lattice."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit clusters are drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster organ (fn-111) is not landed. The inventory's core rating depends on one fruiting reference, and fruit is a seasonal state."}, {"observation": "The trunk is a single, straight or slightly leaning column of near-constant diameter with nothing growing on it.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render is marked 'hidden', so the close-range leaf-base cell cannot be assessed as supplied evidence.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The render has no dead-frond skirt or orange petiole sheath. These secondary traits would add refinement but are not blockers.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The render has a pinnate rosette at the apex, but its fronds are short and mostly straight, forming a compact ball. The long fronds, the arching and recurving sweep, and the hemisphere/shuttlecock outline seen in reference-0 are missing."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render's leaflets are broad, soft and drooping. The references show narrow, stiff, sharp-tipped leaflets at differing angles that give the frond a bristly, plumose look."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render shows a smooth trunk with sparse isolated stubs and no tessellating spiral diamond lattice. This judges what is drawn and invents nothing."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render has no fibre or husk layer; the trunk is a plain dark surface."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render has a single unbranched column of near-constant diameter in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render has no fruit bunches. fn-111 is acknowledged as not landed. The core rating is based on a single seasonal reference, but the mismatch is still recorded."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"e063a8ef-2245-4a88-a05c-5088a9a48e1a","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_command